# DiscoveryBench — gardening pathway prevalence styles across habitat types
## Results summary (evidence for the hypothesis)

### Data
- `temporal_trends_contingency_table.csv`: 12x3 period x pathway counts (Gardening 611 / Unintentional 274 / AgriForest 161). Gardening rose from 16.8% (Before 1500) to 75.2% (1985-2019) of introductions; 65% of all gardening records are 1985-2019.
- `invasion_success_pathways.csv`: 81 species. Gardening 42 / Unintentional 30 / AgriForest 9. Gardening species: 20 Shrub/tree + 18 Perennial fg, mean height 6.5 m, invaded-niche breadth 0.45, mean residence time 86 y. Unintentional: 18 Annual fg, height 1.0 m, breadth 0.75, 9.6 invaded plots avg.
- `invaded_niche_pathways.csv`: 632 plots (unique UTM coords), no missing data; n.gard+n.unint+n.agfo == n.total exactly (169/289/23/481); 441 plots non-invaded; 117 plots with >=1 gardening species.
- `phylogenetic_tree.txt`: Newick, 100 tips; all 81 species present (not used per researcher agreement).

