Frequency (occurrence) and dominance (share) are NOT aligned across habitats
(Spearman r=0.11) => two distinct styles.

### Models
- **Frequency (logistic, n=632, has_gard):** elevation OR=0.29/SD (p<0.001),
  distance.road OR=0.72/SD (p=0.035); urban/cropland/stream/progressive n.s.
  jointly. Univariate: elevation OR=0.23, urban OR=1.85, dist.road OR=0.60.
  Elevation bands: 38.3% (<200 m) - 24.0% (200-500) - 7.9% (500-900) - 0% (>900 m).
  McFadden pR2=0.17. Fisher exact lowland-humanized vs upland-natural: OR=20.2,
  p=4.9e-31.
- **Dominance (weighted binomial GLM, n=191 invaded plots, endog=n.gard, weights=n.total):**
  urban.2009.1000m OR=0.733/SD (p<0.001), cropland.2009.50m OR=0.665/SD (p<0.001),
  distance.road OR=1.224/SD (p<0.001), elevation n.s., progressive n.s. (p=0.086).
  Terciles: cropland high tercile share 0.23 vs baseline 0.37 (p=0.024); urban
  terciles 0.41 -> 0.31; elevation high tercile 0.42 vs 0.34 (p=0.30); MWU
  lowland-humanized vs upland-natural share medians 0.33 vs 1.00 (p=0.082, low n).

### Collinearity
elevation ~ temperature r=-0.96, elevation ~ rainfall r=0.86,
temperature ~ rainfall r=-0.90 (VIF 12.8 / 18.2 / 6.2) -> elevation retained as the
climatic-xeric gradient; temperature and rainfall dropped from joint models.

